# BUILDFLOW – FINANCE & PAYROLL DASHBOARD
## Complete Enterprise Finance, Payroll Processing, Supplier Invoice Management, Expense Approval and Payment Operations

Build a complete, premium, production-style Finance & Payroll Dashboard for BuildFlow, a multi-tenant construction workforce management and site operations SaaS platform.

IMPORTANT: Build this dashboard from scratch. Do not reuse the previous Company Admin, Site Manager, Supervisor or SaaS Super Admin dashboard layouts.

This dashboard is for the finance department of a construction company.

The Finance & Payroll department is responsible for:

1. Employee payroll processing.
2. Daily wage and labour payment calculations.
3. Monthly salary calculations.
4. Overtime and incentive calculations.
5. Employee advances and loan deductions.
6. Payroll verification and approval.
7. Payslip generation.
8. Salary payment processing and reconciliation.
9. Supplier invoice management.
10. Contractor invoice management.
11. Purchase bill verification.
12. Employee reimbursement management.
13. Site expenses.
14. Project budget monitoring.
15. Financial reporting.
16. Tax and statutory compliance.
17. Financial audit records.

Build a functional application, not just static dashboard screens.

Use realistic construction-industry workflows and Indian financial context.

Currency: INR (₹).

All financial calculations must be accurate and traceable.

---

# 1. BUSINESS STRUCTURE AND ROLE CONFIGURATION

BuildFlow supports small, medium and large construction companies.

The Finance & Payroll dashboard must adapt dynamically to company size and assigned permissions.

### Small companies

A small construction company may have:

- One Finance Manager.
- One HR Executive.
- One Company Admin.

The Finance Manager may handle payroll, invoices, expenses and payment operations if authorized.

Do not force companies to create separate finance and payroll accounts.

### Medium companies

Support:

- Finance Manager.
- Payroll Officer.
- Accounts Executive.
- Procurement Accounts Executive.
- HR Manager.

Each user should see the relevant modules according to permissions.

### Large companies

Support:

- Finance Head.
- Payroll Manager.
- Payroll Officer.
- Accounts Payable Manager.
- Accounts Receivable Executive.
- Project Accountant.
- Tax and Compliance Officer.
- Treasury / Payment Officer.
- Internal Auditor.

### Role and permission rules

Company Admin must configure:

- Finance roles.
- Payroll roles.
- Approval hierarchy.
- Project financial access.
- Site financial access.
- Payroll visibility.
- Salary information visibility.
- Payment approval limits.
- Invoice approval limits.
- Export permissions.
- Refund and adjustment permissions.

A Finance Officer must not automatically have access to confidential employee HR records.

A Payroll Officer must not automatically have permission to approve their own payroll.

A person who creates a payment should not automatically be able to approve and release the same payment.

Support configurable maker-checker workflows.

